{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Strays</b> — for wisdom is a straight path, and he who abandons it strays in evil deed." "<b>Path of understanding</b> — and it is an adjective noun, or a verb noun." "<b>Rephaim</b> — the dead." "<b>Will rest</b> — that he will stray no more, or: there will be his resting place, and he will have no portion with the righteous, and this is the correct interpretation."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:24:01.079039439Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}